Subject: [PATCH 8/8] tagger: extend the taxonomy for this deployment, rank tags

The general-purpose categories are KEPT — creative agents genuinely produce
travel/food/shopping content — and extended with ten categories covering what
the infrastructure agents write about. Measured over 776 real stored memories,
topic coverage rises 45% -> 77%.

Validated against that same corpus rather than assumed, which surfaced two
things worth fixing at the same time:

* Ambiguous general keywords pruned. Word boundaries fixed "strips"->trip, but
  not words genuinely present in both domains: a memory STORE, a HEALTH check,
  /HOME/..., "of COURSE", to BOOK, a replication DESTINATION, a Hermes SKILL.
  Misleading general tags on technical text: 162 -> 45.
* Tags are ranked by keyword-hit count instead of an arbitrary slice of a set,
  which was unstable run-to-run whenever a memory matched more categories than
  max_tags.
